>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.del_looper : string -> simpset -> simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named looper from a simpset.

`del_looper name ss` removes the looper `name` added by `add_looper`,
`set_looper` or `looper_ss`. Split rules are removed with `del_split`.

### Failure

Never fails. If `ss` has no looper `name`, issues a warning and returns
`ss`.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val c = Context.snapshot();
>>_ val conj_ss = simpLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC) bool_ss;
>> SIMP_TAC (simpLib.del_looper "conj" conj_ss) [] ([], “p ∧ q”) c;
```

### See also

[`simpLib.add_looper`](#simpLib.add_looper),
[`simpLib.del_split`](#simpLib.del_split).
